# The Weekly Challenge 294 - Lubos Kolouch

Solutions for Task 1 (Consecutive Sequence) and Task 2 (Next Permutation) in Perl and Python.

## Task 1: Consecutive Sequence
- Find the length of the longest consecutive sequence in an unsorted array in $O(N)$ time.
- Uses hash set lookup for $O(1)$ presence check, expanding sequences only from their minimum elements.

## Task 2: Next Permutation
- Rearrange array into lexicographically next greater permutation in $O(N)$ time and $O(1)$ extra space.
- Classic algorithm: find pivot $i$ from right, find successor $j > i$, swap, and reverse suffix.
